ata-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a class="hd__tel" href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>(508) 656-7436</a> <a class="btn hd__cta" href="/contact" data-ev="estimate_cta" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Free estimate</a> <button class="hd__burger" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mnav" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <span data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs></span><span data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs></span> </button> </div> </div> <nav class="mnav" id="mnav" hidden aria-label="Mobile" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a href="/kitchen-remodeling" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Kitchen remodeling</a><a href="/bathroom-remodeling" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Bathroom remodeling</a><a href="/general-renovations" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>General renovations</a><a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Carpentry</a><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Deck building</a><a href="/interior-painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Interior painting</a><a href="/exterior-painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Exterior painting</a><a href="/building-restoration" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Building restoration</a><a href="/water-damage-restoration" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Water damage restoration</a> <hr class="rule" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a href="/painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Painting</a><a href="/portfolio" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Our work</a><a href="/areas-we-serve" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Areas we serve</a> <a href="/about" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>About</a><a href="/contact" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Free estimate</a> <a class="mnav__tel" href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>(508) 656-7436</a> </div> </nav> </header> <script type="module">var e=document.querySelector(`.hd__burger`),t=document.getElementById(`mnav`);e?.addEventListener(`click`,()=>{let n=e.getAttribute(`aria-expanded`)===`true`;e.setAttribute(`aria-expanded`,String(!n)),t&&(t.hidden=n),e.setAttribute(`aria-label`,n?`Open menu`:`Close menu`)});</script> <main id="main" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <section class="top wrap-wide" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <div data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>/</span> <a href="/flooring" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Flooring</a></nav> <h1 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Carpet Installation</h1> <p class="cost" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Typical Central MA range: <strong data-astro-cid-j5amansv>$3.50–$9 per sq ft installed</strong></p> <p class="lead" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Soft, warm and quiet. Bedrooms, finished basements and stairs, with the right pad for each room.</p> <a class="btn" href="#estimate" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Book a free in-home consultation</a> </div> <figure data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <img src="/flooring/carpet-installation-room.webp" alt="Design idea: finished basement family room with oatmeal-colored plush carpet" width="1600" height="1195" fetchpriority="high" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <figcaption data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Design idea (AI illustration) — not an MCB project photo.</figcaption> </figure> </section> <article class="wrap prose" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 id="who-carpet-is-right-for-and-where-it-isnt">Who carpet is right for, and where it isn’t</h2>
<p>Carpet still does something no hard floor can: it’s soft, warm on a January morning and quiet. That is why it keeps its place in bedrooms, playrooms, finished basements and on stairs, where a padded surface is safer for kids and older family members.</p>
<p>Where it doesn’t belong: kitchens, bathrooms, laundry rooms, entries, and any basement that has taken water. Carpet also isn’t a good fit if someone in the house is bothered by dust, or if you have pets that aren’t reliably house-trained. For rooms like those, <a href="/flooring/luxury-vinyl-plank">luxury vinyl plank</a> or <a href="/flooring/laminate-flooring">laminate</a> is the better call.</p>
<h2 id="bedrooms-basements-and-stairs">Bedrooms, basements and stairs</h2>
<p><strong>Bedrooms.</strong> This is carpet’s easiest job. Low traffic, no water, and people like something soft underfoot first thing in the morning. A plush or a textured cut pile with a good pad feels best here.</p>
<p><strong>Finished basements.</strong> A basement family room is where carpet does the most for comfort, because a slab is cold and hard. It’s also where it goes wrong most often. The rules: test the slab, pick a synthetic fiber that won’t feed mildew, use a pad with a moisture barrier, keep a dehumidifier running, and never lay carpet over a slab that has had standing water. Some homeowners add raised subfloor panels first to put an air gap between the slab and the carpet.</p>
<p><strong>Stairs.</strong> Carpeted stairs cut noise and slips. There are two common ways to wrap them: waterfall, where the carpet drops straight from the nose of one tread to the next, and cap-and-band (often called upholstered or Hollywood), where it’s tucked tight under each nose for a tailored look. A runner that leaves painted or stained wood showing at the sides is a third option.</p>
<h2 id="choosing-the-pad">Choosing the pad</h2>
<p>The pad matters more than most people think. It sets how the carpet feels, and a pad that is too soft lets the carpet flex and wear out early.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Rebond foam.</strong> The most common pad. Look at density, not just thickness. Around 6 to 8 lb density at about 7/16 inch is a good general choice.</li>
<li><strong>Memory foam or frothed foam.</strong> Softer feel for bedrooms, at a higher price.</li>
<li><strong>Moisture-barrier pad.</strong> A film on top of the pad keeps spills from soaking through to the subfloor. Worth it in basements and for pet owners.</li>
<li><strong>Stairs.</strong> A thinner, firmer pad so the carpet wraps the nose tightly and doesn’t feel mushy underfoot.</li>
</ul>
<p>Many carpet makers specify the pad their product needs. Following that is part of doing the job right.</p>
<h2 id="choosing-the-carpet">Choosing the carpet</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Fiber.</strong> Nylon holds up best to traffic and springs back after furniture. Polyester (PET) is soft and resists stains but crushes faster in busy areas. Triexta falls in between and handles stains well. Wool is natural and long-lasting but costs more and isn’t a basement fiber.</li>
<li><strong>Style.</strong> Plush looks formal and shows footprints. Textured and frieze hide footprints and vacuum marks. Loop styles like Berber are durable but can snag on pet claws.</li>
<li><strong>Face weight and twist.</strong> Heavier face weight and a tighter twist generally mean the carpet stays looking new longer.</li>
<li><strong>Color.</strong> Mid-tone neutrals hide the most. Very light carpet in a basement next to the back door is a fight you won’t win.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="what-carpet-costs-in-central-ma">What carpet costs in Central MA</h2>
<p>National guides put carpet around $2 to $8 per square foot installed with pad, and Angi lists Boston-area carpet around $3.50 to $11 per square foot. For Central MA, a typical range is about <strong>$3.50 to $9 per square foot installed, pad included</strong>.</p>
<p>Typical ranges, not quotes:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Typical scope</th>
<th>Size</th>
<th>Typical installed range</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>One bedroom, old carpet removed</td>
<td>~144 sq ft</td>
<td>$550–$1,400</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Basement family room over a dry slab</td>
<td>~400 sq ft</td>
<td>$1,500–$3,800</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Straight staircase</td>
<td>~13 steps</td>
<td>$250–$950</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Old carpet and pad removal</td>
<td>per sq ft</td>
<td>add $0.70–$1.60</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Transitions to hard floors</td>
<td>each</td>
<td>add $25–$100</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Stairs are priced per step. Cap-and-band, winders and open-sided stairs sit at the high end. Our written estimate itemises scope, materials and exclusions, including pad type by name.</p>
<h2 id="what-the-job-involves-step-by-step">What the job involves, step by step</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Measure and plan seams.</strong> We measure each room and lay out where seams will fall, keeping them out of doorways and main walking paths where we can.</li>
<li><strong>Moisture check on slabs.</strong> Basements get tested before carpet is ordered.</li>
<li><strong>Demo.</strong> Old carpet, pad and bad tack strip come out and staples are pulled.</li>
<li><strong>Subfloor prep.</strong> Squeaks screwed down, damaged spots repaired, and the floor swept clean.</li>
<li><strong>Tack strip and pad.</strong> New tack strip around the edges, pad laid and seamed, stapled on wood or glued on concrete.</li>
<li><strong>Install and stretch.</strong> Carpet is seamed and then power-stretched so it stays flat instead of rippling in a year.</li>
<li><strong>Stairs and transitions.</strong> Treads and risers fitted by hand, then metal or wood transitions where carpet meets hard floor.</li>
<li><strong>Doors and cleanup.</strong> Doors trimmed if they drag, and debris hauled away.</li>
</ol>
<p>Most bedroom jobs are one day. A basement plus stairs is usually one to two days.</p>
<h2 id="new-england-issues-that-affect-carpet">New England issues that affect carpet</h2>
<p><strong>Basements and radon.</strong> A lot of basements in Central Massachusetts have radon mitigation systems. We leave the suction point and sealed cracks alone and keep access open. Moisture is the bigger risk for carpet specifically, so the slab test isn’t optional.</p>
<p><strong>Hardwood under the carpet.</strong> In older colonials around Lancaster and Bolton, and in many Worcester three-deckers, there’s often oak flooring under wall-to-wall carpet. Before recarpeting, check a closet corner. If the wood is in good shape, <a href="/flooring/hardwood-floor-refinishing">refinishing it</a> may be the better investment, with carpet runners or rugs where you want softness.</p>
<p><strong>Asbestos.</strong> Old carpet in pre-1980s homes sometimes covers 9-inch by 9-inch vinyl tiles or black mastic. Carpet doesn’t require removing them. We test before we tear anything out, and Massachusetts rules for asbestos work, including MassDEP notification before removal, apply if it has to come up.</p>
<p><strong>Narrow, steep stairs.</strong> Older homes in towns like Marlborough often have tight stairways with winders. Those take more cutting and are priced accordingly.</p>
<p><strong>Lead paint.</strong> Pulling painted stair skirt boards or trim in a pre-1978 house falls under EPA RRP rules. Ask any contractor for their RRP paperwork in writing.</p>
<h2 id="what-to-ask-any-flooring-contractor">What to ask any flooring contractor</h2>
<ul>
<li>What pad are you using, and does it meet the carpet maker’s requirements?</li>
<li>Where will the seams be?</li>
<li>Will you power-stretch the carpet?</li>
<li>How are stairs priced, and which style is quoted?</li>
<li>Will you test a basement slab for moisture first?</li>
<li>Is removal and disposal of the old carpet included?</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="next-step">Next step</h2>
<p>If you’re recarpeting bedrooms, a basement or a staircase, we’ll come out for a free in-home consultation: measure, bring carpet and pad samples, and follow up with a written estimate. See the <a href="/flooring">flooring guide</a> to compare other options.</p>
 <section class="faq" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Common questions</h2> <details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Is carpet a good idea in a basement?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>It can be, in a basement that stays dry. We test the slab for moisture, use a synthetic carpet and a pad with a moisture barrier, and recommend running a dehumidifier. If the basement has ever taken on water, a hard floor like vinyl plank is the safer choice.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>What pad should I get?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>For most bedrooms and living rooms, a 7/16-inch rebond pad around 8 lb density is a solid choice. Stairs do better with a thinner, firmer pad. Basements need a pad with a moisture barrier. The carpet maker&#39;s requirements come first.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>How is carpet on stairs priced?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>By the step, because each tread and riser is cut and fastened by hand. A straight staircase is simplest; winders, landings, open sides and spindles add time and cost.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Can you carpet over old floor tile?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Usually, if the tile is flat and firmly stuck down. Tack strip and pad go right over it. If it&#39;s pre-1980s 9-inch tile, covering it is often simpler than removing it, and we test before disturbing it.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>How long does carpet installation take?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>A couple of bedrooms and a hall usually take one day, including removing the old carpet. A large basement or a full floor with stairs may take two.</p></details> </section> </article> <section class="wrap-wide more" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Other flooring ideas</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/flooring/hardwood-floor-installation" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/flooring/hardwood-floor-installation-swatch.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of white oak hardwood planks" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Hardwood Floor Installation</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/flooring/hardwood-floor-refinishing" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/flooring/hardwood-floor-refinishing-swatch.webp" alt="Design idea: oak floor shown half sanded and half stained" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Hardwood Floor Refinishing</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/flooring/luxury-vinyl-plank" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/flooring/luxury-vinyl-plank-swatch.webp" alt="Design idea: luxury vinyl plank samples fanned out showing several oak-look colors" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Luxury Vinyl Plank Flooring Installation</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/flooring/tile-flooring" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/flooring/tile-flooring-swatch.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of grey stone-look porcelain tile" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Tile Flooring Installation</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/flooring/laminate-flooring" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/flooring/laminate-flooring-swatch.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of hickory-look laminate planks" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Laminate Flooring Installation</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/flooring/epoxy-garage-floors" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/flooring/epoxy-garage-floors-swatch.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of grey and black flake epoxy floor coating" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Epoxy Garage and Basement Floors</span></a></li> </ul> <p data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/flooring" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Back to flooring</a></p> </section> <div id="estimate" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><form class="ef" id="estimate-form" novalidate data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-name" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Name <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-name" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Please tell us your name.</p> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-phone" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Phone <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-phone" name="phone" type="tel" inputmode="tel" autocomplete="tel" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-phone" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>We need a phone number to reach you.</p> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-email" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Email</label> <input id="ef-email" name="email" type="email" inputmode="email" autocomplete="email" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-email" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>That email address doesn't look right.</p> </div> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-town" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project town <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-town" name="town" type="text" autocomplete="address-level2" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-town" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Which town is the project in?</p> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-type" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project type <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <select id="ef-type" name="projectType" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option value="" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Choose one…</option> <option value="Kitchen remodeling" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Kitchen remodeling</option><option value="Bathroom remodeling" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Bathroom remodeling</option><option value="General renovations" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>General renovations</option><option value="Carpentry" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Carpentry</option><option value="Deck building" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Deck building</option><option value="Interior painting" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Interior painting</option><option value="Exterior painting" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Exterior painting</option><option value="Building restoration" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Building restoration</option><option value="Water damage restoration" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Water damage restoration</option> <option value="Multiple / not sure" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Multiple, or not sure yet</option> </select> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-type" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Please pick the closest match.</p> </div> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-details" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project details <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <textarea id="ef-details" name="projectDetails" rows="5" required placeholder="What you want done, roughly when, and anything you already know about the space." data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn></textarea> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-details" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>A sentence or two is plenty.</p> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-timing" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Desired timing</label> <select id="ef-timing" name="timing" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option value="" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>No strong preference</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>As soon as possible</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Within 1–3 months</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Within 3–6 months</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Later this year</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Just planning / budgeting</option> </select> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-contact" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Preferred contact</label> <select id="ef-contact" name="preferredContact" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Phone call</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Text message</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Email</option> </select> </div> </div> <!-- Honeypot. Off-screen, aria-hidden, never focusable. --> <div class="ef__hp" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-company" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Company</label> <input id="ef-company" name="company" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> </div> <p class="ef__consent" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>
By sending this you agree we can contact you about your project by phone, text or email.
    Message rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out of texts at any time. We don't sell your details.
</p> <button class="btn ef__submit" type="submit" data-ev="form_submit" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Send it over</button> <p class="ef__note" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>We read every one of these. Prefer to talk?
<a href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>(508) 656-7436</a>.</p> <p class="ef__fail" id="ef-fail" role="alert" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn></p> </form> <div class="ef__ok" id="ef-ok" role="status" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <h3 data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Got it.</h3> <p data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Your details are with us. We'll be in touch to arrange a look at the project.
     If it's urgent, call <a href="tel:+15086567436" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>(508) 656-7436</a>.</p> </div> <script>(function(){const CRM = {"endpoint":"https://backend.leadconnectorhq.com/external-tracking/events","locationId":"b5lmCvdlpVkhC4JOVBjd","trackingId":"tk_e76468050a3e42e0b65b2fa5b3c87a7f"};
const PHONE = "(508) 656-7436";
const EMAIL = "douglas@mcitybuilders.com";

  const form = document.getElementById('estimate-form');
  const okBox = document.getElementById('ef-ok');
  const failBox = document.getElementById('ef-fail');
  if (form) {
    const started = Date.now();
    let announcedStart = false;
    form.addEventListener('input', () => {
      if (!announcedStart && typeof gtag === 'function') {
        announcedStart = true;
        gtag('event', 'form_start', { form_id: 'mcb_estimate' });   // no field contents
      }
    }, { once: false });

    const showErr = (el, on) => {
      el.setAttribute('aria-invalid', String(on));
      const p = form.querySelector('[data-err="' + el.id + '"]');
      if (p) p.hidden = !on;
    };

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      failBox.hidden = true;

      // --- validation with real messages, focus moved to the first problem
      let firstBad = null;
      for (const el of form.querySelectorAll('[required]')) {
        const bad = !el.value.trim();
        showErr(el, bad);
        if (bad && !firstBad) firstBad = el;
      }
      const em = form.querySelector('#ef-email');
      const emBad = em.value.trim() !== '' && !/^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]{2,}$/.test(em.value.trim());
      showErr(em, emBad);
      if (emBad && !firstBad) firstBad = em;
      if (firstBad) { firstBad.focus(); return; }

      // --- bot gates: hidden field filled, or submitted faster than a human types
      const fd = new FormData(form);
      if (String(fd.get('company') || '').trim() !== '' || Date.now() - started < 3000) {
        form.hidden = true; okBox.hidden = false; return;   // silent, nothing sent
      }

      const btn = form.querySelector('.ef__submit');
      const label = btn.textContent;
      btn.textContent = 'Sending…'; btn.disabled = true;

      let ss = null; try { ss = sessionStorage; } catch (_) {}
      const attr = (k) => { try { return (ss && ss.getItem('mcb_' + k)) || ''; } catch (_) { return ''; } };

      const payload = {
        type: 'external_form_submission',
        timestamp: Date.now(),
        formId: 'Estimate Request',
        formData: {
          full_name: fd.get('name'),
          phone: fd.get('phone'),
          email: fd.get('email') || '',          // logical OR. Not a pipe.
          'contact.project_details': fd.get('projectDetails'),
          project_town: fd.get('town'),
          project_type: fd.get('projectType'),
          timing: fd.get('timing') || '',
          preferred_contact: fd.get('preferredContact') || '',
          utm_source: attr('utm_source'), utm_medium: attr('utm_medium'),
          utm_campaign: attr('utm_campaign'), utm_term: attr('utm_term'),
          utm_content: attr('utm_content'), gclid: attr('gclid'), fbclid: attr('fbclid'),
          landing_page: attr('mcb_landing') || attr('landing'),
          referrer: attr('referrer') || document.referrer || '',
          Timezone: Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone,
        },
        url: location.href, title: document.title, path: location.pathname,
        userAgent: navigator.userAgent,
        trackingId: CRM.trackingId, locationId: CRM.locationId,
        sessionId: (crypto && crypto.randomUUID) ? crypto.randomUUID() : String(Math.random()).slice(2),
      };

      let ok = false, diag = '';
      try {
        const res = await fetch(CRM.endpoint, {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', version: '2021-07-28' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        });
        ok = res.ok; diag = 'HTTP ' + res.status;
      } catch (err) { diag = 'network: ' + (err && err.message); }

      if (!ok) {
        // Nothing reached the CRM. Keep every keystroke on screen, give a real
        // route through, and do NOT report a conversion.
        console.error('[MCB estimate form]', diag);
        btn.textContent = label; btn.disabled = false;
        failBox.innerHTML = 'We couldn\'t send that from the website. Please call ' +
          '<a href="tel:+15086567436">' + PHONE + '</a> or email ' +
          '<a href="mailto:' + EMAIL + '">' + EMAIL + '</a>. ' +
          'Everything you typed is still in the form above.';
        failBox.hidden = false;
        failBox.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
        return;
      }

      if (typeof gtag === 'function') {
        gtag('event', 'generate_lead', { form_id: 'mcb_estimate', lead_source: 'website_estimate_form' });
      }
      form.hidden = true; okBox.hidden = false;
      okBox.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
      okBox.querySelector('h3').setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');
      okBox.querySelector('h3').focus();
    });
  }
})();</script></div> </main> <footer class="ft" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="ft__top" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <span class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Maverick City Builders</span> <p class="ft__pitch" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>General contracting and remodeling across Massachusetts.</p> <a class="btn btn--onDark" href="/contact" data-ev="estimate_cta" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Request an estimate</a> </div> <nav aria-label="Services" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Services</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/kitchen-remodeling" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Kitchen remodeling</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/bathroom-remodeling" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Bathroom remodeling</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/general-renovations" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>General renovations</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Carpentry</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Deck building</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/interior-painting" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Interior painting</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/exterior-painting" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Exterior painting</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/building-restoration" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Building restoration</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/water-damage-restoration" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Water damage restoration</a></li></ul> </nav> <nav aria-label="Company" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Company</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/about" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>About</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/portfolio" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Our work</a></li> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/areas-we-serve" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Areas we serve</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/blog" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Articles</a></li> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/contact" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Contact</a></li> </ul> </nav> <div data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Contact</h2> <address class="ft__nap" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <a href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>(508) 656-7436</a> <a href="mailto:douglas@mcitybuilders.com" data-ev="email_click" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>douglas@mcitybuilders.com</a> <span data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>1171 Main St<br data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Lancaster, MA 01523</span> <em data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Office visits by appointment</em> </address> </div> </div> <hr class="rule" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="ft__base" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <p data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>&copy; 2026 Maverick City Builders &middot; Lancaster, Massachusetts</p> <p data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/privacy-policy" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Privacy</a> &middot; <a href="/terms" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Terms</a> &middot;
<a href="/accessibility" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Accessibility</a> &middot; <a href="/cookie-policy" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Cookies</a></p> </div> </div> </footer> </main>  <div id="mcb-cookie-banner" hidden role="dialog" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Cookie choices" style="position:fixed;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:99999;background:#0b0b0b;border-top:2px solid #E10600;color:#e6e6e6;padding:18px 20px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;align-items:center;justify-content:center"> <span style="max-width:640px">We measure page views with Google Analytics in cookieless mode. Accept to allow analytics cookies and ad measurement; Decline to stay cookieless. Read our <a href="/cookie-policy" style="color:#ff6b6b;text-decoration:underline">Cookie Policy</a>.</span> <span style="display:flex;gap:10px"> <button type="button" id="mcb-cookie-decline" style="background:transparent;color:#e6e6e6;border:1px solid #777;padding:12px 20px;min-height:44px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">Decline</button> <button type="button" id="mcb-cookie-accept" style="background:#E10600;color:#fff;border:0;padding:12px 22px;min-height:44px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">Accept</button> </span> </div> <!-- Analytics with Google Consent Mode (mcb-consent-v2, 2026-09-18, Doug's decision).
       GA4 loads by default with analytics_storage DENIED = cookieless pings, no _ga cookie.
       Accept upgrades consent to granted. Browsers sending Do-Not-Track or Global Privacy
       Control get nothing at all. The static site does the same via patch_consent.py. --> <script>(function(){const ga4 = "G-7HXJQJL5Q2";

    (function () {
      var KEY = 'mcb-consent'; // MUST match the static site's key (hyphen). An underscore here meant GA4 never loaded on any Astro page.
      var dnt = false;
      try { dnt = navigator.doNotTrack == '1' || window.doNotTrack == '1' || !!navigator.globalPrivacyControl; } catch (e) {}
      window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
      window.gtag = function () { window.dataLayer.push(arguments); };
      gtag('consent', 'default', { ad_storage: 'denied', ad_user_data: 'denied', ad_personalization: 'denied',
        analytics_storage: 'denied', functionality_storage: 'granted', security_storage: 'granted' });
      function load() {
        if (window.__mcbTagged) return; window.__mcbTagged = true;
        var s = document.createElement('script'); s.async = true;
        s.src = 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=' + ga4;
        document.head.appendChild(s);
        gtag('js', new Date()); gtag('config', ga4);
      }
      function boot() { // Accept: cookies + ad measurement allowed
        gtag('consent', 'update', { ad_storage: 'granted', ad_user_data: 'granted', ad_personalization: 'granted', analytics_storage: 'granted' });
        load();
      }
      var stored = null;
      try { stored = localStorage.getItem(KEY); } catch (e) {}
      if (stored === 'granted') boot();
      else if (!dnt) load(); // undecided or declined: cookieless measurement only
      window.__mcbConsentBoot = boot;
      // Same banner as the static site. Without it a visitor who LANDS on a town page
      // is never asked, so is never measured.
      try {
        var v = localStorage.getItem(KEY), b = document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-banner');
        if (b && v !== 'granted' && v !== 'denied') {
          b.hidden = false;
          document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-accept').addEventListener('click', function () { try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, 'granted'); } catch (e) {} b.hidden = true; boot(); });
          document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-decline').addEventListener('click', function () { try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, 'denied'); } catch (e) {} b.hidden = true; });
        }
      } catch (e) {}
      // lightweight, non-sensitive interaction events
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var a = e.target && e.target.closest && e.target.closest('[data-ev]');
        if (a && typeof window.gtag === 'function') {
          gtag('event', a.getAttribute('data-ev'), { link_url: a.getAttribute('href') || '' });
        }
      }, true);
    })();
  })();</script></body> </html>